    "updated_at": "2023-04-19T08:41:59Z",
    "body": "First, when using width descriptors, which seems to be the case here (assuming you mean `w` instead of `px` in your example), the `src` attribute is not added to the source set as a candidate. See https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#create-a-source-set step 4\r\n\r\nThe reason it's required is for backwards compatibility with old browsers and other UAs (e.g. search engines) that don't implement `srcset` or `picture`. This is explained in the introduction here https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#introduction-3:viewport-based-selection-2\r\n\r\n> For backwards compatibility, one of the URLs is specified in the [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element's [src](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-img-src) attribute. In new user agents, the [src](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-img-src) attribute is ignored when the [srcset](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-img-srcset) attribute uses w descriptors.\r\n\r\nHowever, `srcset` has now [existed in the spec for over a decade](https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/969543cd259a0cc41a0a5cbe97e0010c6999eb09) and [`picture` almost a decade](61b568a581ffa526d0061444b7d1ae258719a66c), we could indeed revisit this requirement. What is the current status for non-browser image-fetching UAs?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
